<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n16687" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀστῠ-άναξ</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾰν], <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ακτος</span>, ὁ,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>lord of the city,</i> epith.
			of certain gods, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Supp.</u>
				1018
			</span></i> (lyr.): in <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> only as pr. n., <i>Astyanax,</i> the son of
			Hector:—hence Adj.
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀστυανάκτειος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				9.351
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Leon.
			</span></i>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> by an
			obscene pun, 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄστυτος</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Eust.
				849.54
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b> name of a
				<i>fish,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i></div>
